<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02UV">Remark <span data-tag="02UV">7.4.5.14</span>.</a> In the statement of Theorem <a data-tag="02UU" href="/tag/02UU">7.4.5.13</a>, the covariant refraction diagram $\mathrm{Rf}: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}_{ {\bf 1} }$ and the covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{ \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright } }: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ are only well-defined up to isomorphism (as objects of the $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}, \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}_{ {\bf 1} })$ and $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda } )$, respectively). However, the hypothesis and conclusion of the theorem depend only on their isomorphism classes (see Exercise <a data-tag="02SW" href="/tag/02SW">6.3.1.11</a> and Corollary <a data-tag="02K1" href="/tag/02K1">7.1.3.19</a>). </p>
